
Incarnate
April 17, 2014	· by narcolapser	· Bookmark the permalink. ·

Image

It has been very busy since January, and I have three lovely young ladies here to thank for that.

Sarah, Audra, and Aseneth arrived with the last intake here at Lifehope Training Center in January. They are our dance interns, a new program for us, and their time is coming to a close in these next few weeks. But before I get to the exciting near future, let me share a little about our wonderful Interns.

The interns are here as part of a larger program done by OM Arts called Incarnate, you can read more about Incarnate at http://www.arts.om.org/school. For a myriad of reasons, the dance program did not happen as part of Incarnate. So instead, they came here where Amy, Myself, and for a while Thalita, poured into these three amazing dancers.

They came here, having years of dance experience. In classical ballet they are far above my skill level. This was hard for me for a while. I felt inept. Here I am suppose to be one of their teachers, and I feel like I’ve got about 15 left feet, each wishing they were ears. But “If the whole body were an eye, where would the hearing be? If the whole body were hearing, where would the sense of smell be?” (1 Cor 12:17) I had my time in the sun when we got to hip-hop and street styles for which they had precious little instruction. My dozen or so left feet found their footing as I spun around on the floor in our break dancing class.

dance team pic

We had one dance track student this term as well, Lenka from the Czech Republic. We had all six of us together for the normal dance track lessons, the theology of arts, and reasons why God calls us to minister through arts. But unlike our dance track students they had their entire time devoted to their internship while the dance track students have other responsibilities beyond dance. My time with them was centered around these studies.

They and Amy went through an extra book just themselves called “Heart of the Artist”. (Having a male in the group would have changed the dynamic. Besides, I had to go figure out why the internet wasn’t working.) They’ve told me a little of their discussions, but you wouldn’t have to be told to know that God has been working in these girls. I’ve seen them come as amazing dedicated artists who love God and become amazing Women of Christ with a God given passion for arts. None of them were Prima Donnas when they came, just nice young women. Now I see three servants whose hearts are broken for the world and prepared to spread the love of God through dance.

This Saturday, the 19th, we fly out for Forterocca in Bobbio, Italy. There we will meet up with the rest of Incarnate for the final week of their program. We will jump in as dancers to accompany the visual artists, musicians, and actors. We’ll get a chance to hear what God has been sharing with them and a chance to tell them what God has shared with us. And then we will go out into that community to share with the Italians the love of God through the arts.

We’ll be there for ten days. And when all the tears of parting have been shed, three young women with faith and talent hand in hand will return to the United States where they will bless those around them.

Pray for our work. All of us in the Dance team as we rapidly finish all the choreography for the pieces we’ll be performing in Italy.

Pray for our health. The enemy hates when the love of God is spread. He hates it even more when it’s artists who are out to touch the hearts of those who hear and see. Pray for energy and that no one gets injured or sick.

Pray for our hearts. As I’m writing this I can feel the deceiver trying to stir doubt. I’m not a good enough dancer he tells me. But all things are possible through Christ who strengths me. This is just the start of the attacks that are bound to hit us. Send your prayers of protection with us; we’ll need them.

Pray for their souls. Let the soil be good that the good news is scattered upon. Linda Wells who started OM-Dancelink said that we artists come along to “clear the birds” to keep them from the seeds that are scattered.

Pray for Lifehope. With me in Italy, Kees-Jan doing holiday clubs with Kids n’ Things, the IT department is spread very thin right now.

God bless; it is certainly a blessing to me to have all your prayers.

Toby

